-- Indistinguishability Obfuscator (iO) specification over a semantic fiber:
-- Given an adversary distinguisher D : C -> Obs and compiler O : (A -> B) -> C,
-- O satisfies ideal fiber-indistinguishability wrt D iff any two programs on the same
-- semantic fiber produce identical observable distributions under D.
IdealFiberIO : {A B C Obs : Type} → ((A → B) → C) → (C → Obs) → Type
IdealFiberIO {A} {B} obf adv =
  (p0 p1 : A → B) → SemFiber p0 p1 → adv (obf p0) ≡ adv (obf p1)
